 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Battery State of Health (SoH) Prediction Demo\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates the complete workflow for predicting battery State of Health using LSTM networks.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Project Overview\n",
    "- **Objective**: Predict battery degradation and Remaining Useful Life (RUL)\n",
    "- **Method**: Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) Neural Networks\n",
    "- **Application**: Electric Vehicle (EV) Battery Health Monitoring\n",
    "\n",
    "## Key Features\n",
    "- Data preprocessing and sequence generation\n",
    "- LSTM architecture with attention mechanism\n",
    "- Comprehensive evaluation metrics\n",
    "- Interactive visualizations\n",
    "- RUL prediction based on SoH thresholds"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Import necessary libraries\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from datetime import datetime\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add src directory to path\n",
    "sys.path.append('src')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Import project modules\n",
    "from src.data_preprocessing import BatteryDataProcessor\n",
    "from src.lstm_model import BatterySoHPredictor\n",
    "from src.visualization import BatteryVisualizer\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Libraries imported successfully!\")\n",
    "print(f\"TensorFlow version: {tf.__version__}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Data Loading and Preprocessing\n",
    "\n",
    "First, we'll load and preprocess the battery cycle data. The system can work with real battery data or generate synthetic data for demonstration."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Initialize data processor\n",
    "processor = BatteryDataProcessor(\n",
    "    sequence_length=50,\n",
    "    feature_columns=[\n",
    "        'voltage', 'current', 'temperature', 'capacity',\n",
    "        'cycle_number', 'discharge_time', 'charge_time'\n",
    "    ]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load data (will generate sample data if no file exists)\n",
    "print(\"Loading battery data...\")\n",
    "df = processor.load_data(\"data/battery_data.csv\")\n",
    "df = processor.clean_data(df)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nDataset shape: {df.shape}\")\n",
    "print(\"\\nFirst few rows:\")\n",
    "df.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Display data statistics\n",
    "stats = processor.get_data_statistics(df)\n",
    "print(\"Data Statistics:\")\n",
    "for feature, stat in stats.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n{feature}:\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Mean: {stat['mean']:.4f}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Std:  {stat['std']:.4f}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Min:  {stat['min']:.4f}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Max:  {stat['max']:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize raw data\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 3, figsize=(18, 10))\n",
    "axes = axes.flatten()\n",
    "\n",
    "features_to_plot = ['voltage', 'current', 'temperature', 'capacity', 'soh']\n",
    "colors = ['blue', 'green', 'red', 'purple', 'orange']\n",
    "\n",
    "for i, (feature, color) in enumerate(zip(features_to_plot, colors)):\n",
    "    if feature in df.columns:\n",
    "        axes[i].plot(df['cycle_number'], df[feature], color=color, linewidth=2)\n",
    "        axes[i].set_title(f'{feature.replace(\"_\", \" \").title()} vs Cycle')\n",
    "        axes[i].set_xlabel('Cycle Number')\n",
    "        axes[i].set_ylabel(feature.replace(\"_\", \" \").title())\n",
    "        axes[i].grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Remove extra subplot\n",
    "axes[-1].remove()\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Sequence Generation and Data Splitting\n",
    "\n",
    "LSTM networks require sequential data. We'll create sequences from the time series data and split them into training, validation, and test sets."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create LSTM sequences\n",
    "print(\"Creating LSTM sequences...\")\n",
    "X, y = processor.create_sequences(df)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Sequences created:\")\n",
    "print(f\"X shape: {X.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"y shape: {y.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Sequence length: {X.shape[1]}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Number of features: {X.shape[2]}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Split data into train, validation, and test sets\n",
    "X_train, X_val, X_test, y_train, y_val, y_test = processor.split_data(X, y)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Data split:\")\n",
    "print(f\"Training set:   {X_train.shape[0]} sequences\")\n",
    "print(f\"Validation set: {X_val.shape[0]} sequences\")\n",
    "print(f\"Test set:       {X_test.shape[0]} sequences\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. LSTM Model Building\n",
    "\n",
    "We'll build a sophisticated LSTM architecture with multiple layers, batch normalization, and dropout for regularization."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Initialize LSTM predictor\n",
    "predictor = BatterySoHPredictor(\n",
    "    sequence_length=50,\n",
    "    n_features=7\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Build the LSTM model\n",
    "print(\"Building LSTM model...\")\n",
    "model = predictor.build_model(\n",
    "    lstm_units=[128, 64, 32],\n",
    "    dropout_rate=0.3,\n",
    "    learning_rate=0.001\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Display model architecture\n",
    "print(\"\\nModel Architecture:\")\n",
    "print(predictor.get_model_summary())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Model Training\n",
    "\n",
    "Train the LSTM model with early stopping and learning rate scheduling."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Train the model\n",
    "print(\"Training LSTM model...\")\n",
    "history = predictor.train(\n",
    "    X_train, y_train, X_val, y_val,\n",
    "    epochs=100,\n",
    "    batch_size=32,\n",
    "    patience=15\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nTraining completed!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Plot training history\n",
    "predictor.plot_training_history()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Model Evaluation\n",
    "\n",
    "Evaluate the trained model on the test set with comprehensive metrics."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Make predictions on test set\n",
    "print(\"Making predictions on test set...\")\n",
    "y_pred_scaled = predictor.predict(X_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Inverse transform to original scale\n",
    "y_test_orig = processor.inverse_transform_predictions(y_test)\n",
    "y_pred_orig = processor.inverse_transform_predictions(y_pred_scaled)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Predictions shape: {y_pred_orig.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Calculate evaluation metrics\n",
    "metrics = predictor.evaluate(X_test, y_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Evaluation Metrics:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 40)\n",
    "for metric, value in metrics.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"{metric.upper():<10}: {value:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 40)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Visualization of Results\n",
    "\n",
    "Create comprehensive visualizations to analyze model performance."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Initialize visualizer\n",
    "visualizer = BatteryVisualizer()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot predictions vs actual values\n",
    "visualizer.plot_predictions(y_test_orig, y_pred_orig, title=\"Test Set: SoH Predictions\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Plot degradation curves\n",
    "visualizer.plot_degradation_curve(y_test_orig, y_pred_orig)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Plot residuals\n",
    "visualizer.plot_residuals(y_test_orig, y_pred_orig)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Remaining Useful Life (RUL) Prediction\n",
    "\n",
    "Predict the remaining useful life based on SoH thresholds."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Predict RUL with 80% SoH threshold\n",
    "threshold = 0.8\n",
    "rul_predictions = predictor.predict_rul(X_test, threshold)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"RUL Predictions (threshold = {threshold:.0%}):\")\n",
    "print(f\"Mean RUL: {np.mean(rul_predictions):.1f} cycles\")\n",
    "print(f\"Std RUL:  {np.std(rul_predictions):.1f} cycles\")\n",
    "print(f\"Min RUL:  {np.min(rul_predictions):.1f} cycles\")\n",
    "print(f\"Max RUL:  {np.max(rul_predictions):.1f} cycles\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Plot RUL distribution\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "plt.hist(rul_predictions, bins=30, alpha=0.7, color='skyblue', edgecolor='black')\n",
    "plt.axvline(np.mean(rul_predictions), color='red', linestyle='--', \n",
    "            label=f'Mean: {np.mean(rul_predictions):.1f} cycles')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Remaining Useful Life (cycles)')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Frequency')\n",
    "plt.title(f'RUL Distribution (EOL Threshold: {threshold:.0%})')\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Interactive Dashboard\n",
    "\n",
    "Create an interactive dashboard for exploring the results."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create interactive dashboard\n",
    "cycles_test = np.arange(len(y_test_orig))\n",
    "visualizer.plot_interactive_dashboard(y_test_orig, y_pred_orig, cycles_test)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Model Comparison (Optional)\n",
    "\n",
    "Compare different model architectures if desired."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Build attention-based model for comparison\n",
    "print(\"Building attention-based model...\")\n",
    "attention_predictor = BatterySoHPredictor(sequence_length=50, n_features=7)\n",
    "attention_model = attention_predictor.build_attention_model(\n",
    "    lstm_units=[128, 64],\n",
    "    dropout_rate=0.3,\n",
    "    learning_rate=0.001\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Train attention model\n",
    "print(\"Training attention model...\")\n",
    "attention_history = attention_predictor.train(\n",
    "    X_train, y_train, X_val, y_val,\n",
    "    epochs=50,\n",
    "    batch_size=32,\n",
    "    patience=10\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Evaluate attention model\n",
    "attention_metrics = attention_predictor.evaluate(X_test, y_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nModel Comparison:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 50)\n",
    "print(f\"{'Metric':<15} {'LSTM':<10} {'LSTM+Attention':<15}\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 50)\n",
    "for metric in ['mse', 'mae', 'r2_score']:\n",
    "    lstm_val = metrics[metric]\n",
    "    att_val = attention_metrics[metric]\n",
    "    print(f\"{metric.upper():<15} {lstm_val:<10.4f} {att_val:<15.4f}\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 50)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 10. Save Model and Results\n",
    "\n",
    "Save the trained model and results for future use."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Save the best model\n",
    "model_save_path = \"models/battery_soh_model.h5\"\n",
    "predictor.save_model(model_save_path)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save results\n",
    "import json\n",
    "\n",
    "results = {\n",
    "    \"timestamp\": datetime.now().isoformat(),\n",
    "    \"model_type\": \"LSTM\",\n",
    "    \"sequence_length\": 50,\n",
    "    \"n_features\": 7,\n",
    "    \"metrics\": {k: float(v) for k, v in metrics.items()},\n",
    "    \"rul_stats\": {\n",
    "        \"mean\": float(np.mean(rul_predictions)),\n",
    "        \"std\": float(np.std(rul_predictions)),\n",
    "        \"min\": float(np.min(rul_predictions)),\n",
    "        \"max\": float(np.max(rul_predictions))\n",
    "    }\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "with open(\"results/demo_results.json\", \"w\") as f:\n",
    "    json.dump(results, f, indent=2)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Model saved to: {model_save_path}\")\n",
    "print(\"Results saved to: results/demo_results.json\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "This demo demonstrated:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Data Processing**: Loading and preprocessing battery cycle data\n",
    "2. **Sequence Generation**: Creating time series sequences for LSTM\n",
    "3. **Model Architecture**: Building sophisticated LSTM networks\n",
    "4. **Training**: Training with early stopping and optimization\n",
    "5. **Evaluation**: Comprehensive metrics and analysis\n",
    "6. **Visualization**: Interactive plots and dashboards\n",
    "7. **RUL Prediction**: Estimating remaining useful life\n",
    "8. **Model Comparison**: Comparing different architectures\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Results:\n",
    f"- **R² Score**: {metrics['r2_score']:.4f}\n",
    f"- **MAE**: {metrics['mae']:.4f}\n",
    f"- **RMSE**: {metrics['rmse']:.4f}\n",
    f"- **Mean RUL**: {np.mean(rul_predictions):.1f} cycles\n",
    "\n",
    "The model successfully predicts battery State of Health and can be used for real-time monitoring and predictive maintenance in electric vehicles."
   ]
  }
 ],
